":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tabatkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T23:29:47Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T23:29:47Z","body":"Yeah, that falls right out of the definition. We can add it as an example if needed.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/3994209729/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4005907568","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12735#issuecomment-4005907568","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12735","id":4005907568,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM7uxUxw","user":{"login":"svgeesus","id":2506926,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDY5MjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2506926?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus","html_url":"https://github.com/svgeesus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/svgeesus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T15:31:39Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T15:31:39Z","body":"@zrhoffman could you send a PR to add such an example?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4005907568/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4040186968","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12735#issuecomment-4040186968","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12735","id":4040186968,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAI0trM7w0FxY","user":{"login":"css-meeting-bot","id":27466577,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDY2NTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27466577?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/css-meeting-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/css-meeting-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T15:50:14Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T15:50:14Z","body":"The CSS Working Group just discussed ``[css-properties-values-api] `light-dark()` and system colors in initial values``, and agreed to the following:\n\n* `RESOLVED: Add an example as to why this case is computationally independent`\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;ydaniv> TabAtkins: props and values API says initial values have to be computationally independent<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... question is does this mean that stuff like color scheme are not computationally independent?<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... answer is yes, I don't think we need to add anything, it follows the definition<br>\n&lt;miriam> q+<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... since someone thought this is unclear, we could add a note<br>\n&lt;weinig> q+<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... I think we can resolve close no change<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> dbaron: what's the current state of computed scheme colors?<br>\n&lt;weinig> q-<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> emilio: I think we ended up computes to color<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> system colors compute to color values<br>\n&lt;dbaron> s/computed scheme/the computed value of system colors.  Does it compute to keywords or to/<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack miriam<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> miriam: I think that's right in existing spec, my question is do we need to keep this restriction?<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... it's not the way authors think about custom properties<br>\n&lt;emilio> q+<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... if we don't need it we should not have it<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack emilio<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> emilio: it would be quite weird<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... it's a restriction custom properties is known to have, I'd have to think how easy it is to remove this restriction<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> TabAtkins: we have some color stuff here that is used as initial values in custom properties, but between the color property itself and several other properties which depend on other properties, it's a funky case<br>\n&lt;emilio> color is also not quite that, because currentcolor computes to itself<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... however, outside of color where we do use initial value like em it's calculated like initial em<br>\n&lt;emilio> q+<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... it seems weird to authors it's not resolving the same as set on the element they set it on<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> miriam: I get the complexity, but authors don't have a good way to set a global initial defaults<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... it needs a lot more teaching, or some better way to help authors set both, global defaults that can be relative, and initial value<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> TabAtkins: would love to chat more on the use-cases, and see what are your expectations<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack dbaron<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> dbaron: one thought is what an initial value means is different between inherited and non-inherited<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... on inherited it's used only on the root, as opposed to non-inherited<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... if you wanted this it would be harder to work around the non-inherited ones<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack fantasai<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack emilio<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> astearns: miriam would want to discuss the general authoring problems here?<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> miriam: will open a new one<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> astearns: so for this resolution we decide to add an example?<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> TabAtkins: yeah<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> PROPOSED RESOLUTION: Add an example as to why this case is computationally independent<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> astearns: objections?<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> RESOLVED: Add an example as to why this case is computationally independent<br>\n</details>\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4040186968/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/comments/4066567037","html_url":"https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12735#issuecomment-4066567037","is